<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00059</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>8f45ba6d-3465-420f-b8fa-4ce8a1d48805</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">For questions 1 – 5, use the following scenario to identify the expression, equation, or inequality described.</para>
      <para id="para-00002"><quote id="quote-00001">To support a local senior citizens center, a student club sent a flier home to the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> students in the school. The flier said, “Please bring in money to support the senior citizens center. Paper money and coins accepted!” Their goal is to raise <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> dollars.</quote></para>
      <para id="para-00003">Choose the expression, equation, or inequality, from the list, that describes the given quantity.</para>
      <exercise id="c5eb8b61-7fbc-4523-a1ec-a4cc7ec0eba3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004"> The dollar amount the club would have if they reached half of their goal.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00006"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00007"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00008"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00009"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00010"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00011">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> equals the total dollar amount of the goal. Half that amount is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>.5</m:mi><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00013">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="c30ec0ed-0821-4c1b-8232-b1d7ee553524" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00014"> The dollar amount the club would have if every student at the school donated 50 cents to the cause.</para>
          <para id="para-00015">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00016"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00017"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00018"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00020"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00021">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> equals the total number of students. Fifty cents equals .50, so the total amount raised if all students brought .50 is |(.5n\).</para>
          <para id="para-00022">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00023">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8568a3fb-10b2-47c9-b1fb-06e433a3f9c2" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00024"> The dollar amount the club could donate if they made $50 more than their goal</para>
          <para id="para-00025">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00026"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00027"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00028"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00029"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00030"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00031">Correct! $50 more than the goal of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00032">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00033">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_2cd99f9f-a7a8-4eaf-81ad-a2addfafc27b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00034"> The dollar amount the club would still need to raise to reach its goal after every student at the school donated 50 cents</para>
          <para id="para-00035">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00036"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00037"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00038"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00039"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00040"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00041">Correct! If each student, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, raises .50 that is .50n. To determine how much is left to raise of the goal, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, you could calculate \(T -.50n.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00043">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_0ff9050c-4f35-4b15-9898-adc0d7584f0c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00044"> The dollar amount the club would have if half of the students at the school each gave 50 cents</para>
          <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00046"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>50</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00047"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>T</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00048"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00049"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00050"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>T</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00051">Correct! Half of the students, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, would be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. If they only raised .50 each, it would be <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>9.5</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.50</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>.25</m:mi><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00053">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>0.25</m:mn><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_9a678a3e-ae5c-4af0-8b8b-767aba5e2bbb" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00054">Write an expression that represents the amount of flour required for one cake.</para>
          <para id="para-00055"> Each of the 10 students in the baking club made 2 chocolate cakes for a fundraiser. They all used the same recipe, using <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> cups of flour in total.</para>
          <para id="para-00056">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00059"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00060"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>10</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00061">Correct! If 10 students are making 2 cakes, they need to have 20 equal parts for an answer of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00062">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00063">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mi>c</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>20</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00064">For questions 7 - 8, determine if each is an expression or an equation that represents the English phrase</para>
      <exercise id="_2d9c7397-563f-467a-b604-3775cea9aa44" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00065"> 3(<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> − 7) = 27</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00066">Correct! This is an equation because it has an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00067">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00068">The correct answer is equation.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_827ac3ee-90d0-4c8e-aa3e-5b7472aa4691" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00069"> 5(4<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>− 2) − 7</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00070">Correct! This is an expression because it doesn’t have an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>=</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00071">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00072">The correct answer is expression.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <para id="para-00073">For questions 9 - 10, choose the algebraic expression that represents the English phrase</para>
      <exercise id="_143f01d5-22fa-4aa0-bb7a-c47383bb89b6" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00074">the difference of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> ² and 13</para>
          <para id="para-00075">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00076"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00077"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00078"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>13</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00079"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>13</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00080">Correct! The difference between two numbers is a subtraction problem.</para>
          <para id="para-00081">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00082">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>14</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>13</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. You seem to be stuck who can you ask for help?</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="dccb07a2-39b9-4bbc-9703-6c1e266a5690" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00083">the quotient of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and 2</para>
          <para id="para-00084">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00085"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00086"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00087"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00088"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00089">Correct! The quotient of two numbers is a division problem.</para>
          <para id="para-00090">Try again. Revisit activity 1.1.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00091"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
